('96ee0bae-1d0d-4095-9174-37e703bcd93d', 'Why must healthcare workers verify a patient’s identity before taking vital signs?', '[\"To save time\",\"To ensure the correct patient receives the procedure and avoid errors\",\"To reduce communication\",\"To complete tasks faster\"]', 1, 'a9481fb6-2854-4cb3-ac30-f2a006c80026'),
('9737ac67-4744-4ba6-98df-e97e39a64242', 'Which of the following is a way to break the chain of infection?', '[\"Covering your nose when coughing.\",\"Sharing personal items between residents.\",\"Leaving spills on the floor.\",\"Keeping the same mask on all day.\"]', 0, '3ae10c6f-51c4-4de3-ac3b-45598d7d71b1'),
('97bb9d6f-984f-40fb-8cc8-48d960285c7d', 'What should be done before placing a bedpan under a resident?', '[\"Remove gloves\",\"Lower side rails\",\"Put on gloves and prepare supplies\",\"Leave the room\"]', 2, 'b374df12-e163-42fa-a7a3-de3fcf52ed6a'),
('994e4588-0cac-4fd3-824f-3626bb7c74de', 'A person is a diabetic. You should do the following except…', '[\"Serve their meals and snacks late\",\"You should always check their tray to see what they ate\",\"Let the nurse know whether they ate or not\",\"Provide a between-meal nourishment as the nurse directs\"]', 0, '067af97e-29b0-4d1a-9f2a-76bb5d68f2da'),
('99aa4aa0-a59f-444b-a667-0337eeb03b6f', 'What is one important rule for effective verbal communication?', '[\"Speak as fast as possible\",\"Face the person and speak clearly\",\"Use slang language\",\"Ask many questions at once\"]', 1, 'c595624f-18fa-4978-960d-601f5743654e');
INSERT INTO `Question` (`id`, `text`, `options`, `correctAnswer`, `quizId`) VALUES
('99c96a52-3ba8-4683-981d-c625bc53012f', 'How do consistent infection control practices specifically impact the relationship between patients and the healthcare system?', '[\"They allow patients to diagnose their own illnesses\",\"They help maintain patient trust by providing care in a safe environment\",\"They ensure that all patients receive the same medication\",\"They eliminate the need for patients to provide a medical history\"]', 1, '5e2be435-8690-4235-9548-bc0c6906e02c'),
('99e66d3d-ca0b-408e-89dd-af2384f3781e', 'How often should immobile patients generally be repositioned?', '[\"Once a day\",\"Every two hours\",\"Every 12 hours\",\"Only when they complain\"]', 1, 'a48b15ad-ec69-4d7a-aae3-43a2ff0b4b0f'),
('9a1a2eeb-d6de-4890-b216-3bf1d59ec0f9', 'The nurse spends too much time on research and neglects patient care. This act would be:', '[\"Unethical because the basic responsibility is patient care\",\"Unethical because only doctors do research\",\"Ethical because research is a primary duty\",\"Ethical because it helps more people\"]', 0, '901e5737-19aa-41c8-a13a-cc963b5f734c'),
('9a6af155-bb46-43cc-a28c-12309b3f3b63', 'Why might individuals with limited financial resources experience poor nutrition?', '[\"They eat too much protein\",\"They only drink water\",\"They may rely on low-cost foods lacking essential nutrients\",\"They avoid all carbohydrates\"]', 2, 'c8237a4e-a5c6-44ce-bfbf-7cb1e6093418'),
('9affdaa9-d603-43f6-b35e-65ab3e72ce60', 'Why is communication important during a lift transfer?', '[\"To pass time\",\"To confuse the patient\",\"To coordinate movement and ensure patient understanding and safety\",\"To delay the process\"]', 2, '20efff82-6d52-4bd6-b13a-21418d0239af'),
('9b485dbd-fa1f-49d4-a3c7-d13dc8b855fc', 'Which statement about bed rails is false?', '[\"The nurse and care plan tell you when to raise the bed rails.\",\"Bed rails are considered restraints.\",\"You may leave a person alone when the bed is raised and the bed rails are down.\",\"Bed rails can present hazards because people try to climb over them.\"]', 2, '2d454161-7461-4f34-bb59-00c45483349b'),
('9b4dab25-d879-4f7f-a2d9-9f4d3260827e', 'Why is mild cognitive impairment (MCI) important to recognize?', '[\"It always leads to severe dementia\",\"It has no impact on future health\",\"It may be an early warning sign of dementia but does not always progress\",\"It completely disables a person immediately\"]', 2, 'f7cf8a63-4e75-49d5-918a-6e8dd3e566c3'),
('9b7ff08a-b63c-4f8c-8676-f2b7ccac2ae1', 'Restraints have a very negative impact on the patient’s quality of life both emotionally and physically.', '[\"True\",\"False\",\"Sometimes\",\"None of the above\"]', 0, 'f11f8615-5686-41c1-a549-34a649f9c6a4'),
('9bb048a8-0bb8-4007-9ca7-0cea9dcf05e9', 'Which of the following is an example of protecting patient privacy?', '[\"Discussing a patient in the cafeteria\",\"Sharing medical details with friends\",\"Only discussing patient information with the healthcare team involved in care \",\"Leaving records open on a computer\"]', 2, '22ce5fde-f7e9-4180-b8a7-e490c6d72822'),
('9c6e201b-a15b-4451-b9a4-bd8a3982642b', 'You are caring for a person with dementia, you…', '[\"Share the information about the person’s care.\",\"Share the information about the person’s condition.\",\"Protect confidential information.\",\"Expose the person’s body during care.\"]', 2, '208abab1-1f76-4904-bc79-331e30d79ecc'),
('9ca1572b-b874-4b0b-9383-052f85df3acb', 'What is the correct procedure for dressing a resident who has physical weakness on one side of their body?', '[\"Put clothing on the strong side first\",\"Put clothing on the weak side first\",\"Only use hospital gowns for these residents\",\"Dress both sides at the exact same time\"]', 1, 'e91faa50-7c0d-44f2-bd21-1eaea0a111cf'),
('9cfe40c9-3292-42e2-9b71-0f711b098ca3', 'What is an example of non-verbal communication?', '[\"Writing a report\",\"Speaking on the phone\",\"Facial expressions and gestures\",\"Sending an email\"]', 2, 'c595624f-18fa-4978-960d-601f5743654e'),
('9d712e35-5ae7-4d3d-8713-6e5a5a5c99b5', 'What are height and weight used for in healthcare?', '[\"Only for records\",\"To assess overall health status and physical condition\",\"To replace vital signs\",\"To reduce patient care\"]', 1, '1fdd9048-c2e0-4125-a91e-19d9e6eb3a5f'),
('9dc1791f-6642-4140-8c44-97ae2b1b9445', 'What is a common communication barrier in healthcare?', '[\"Speaking clearly\",\"Using simple language\",\"Impaired hearing\",\"Maintaining eye contact\"]', 2, 'fcb31254-4d0b-466f-9a46-176b4e54a3ab'),
('9dd678b9-3d02-4237-bb16-566231d6ec81', 'What is the most important reason for a caregiver to wash their hands before beginning grooming care?', '[\"To save time during the procedure\",\"To prevent the spread of microbes and protect the patient from infection\",\"To make the patient feel more comfortable\",\"To keep their own skin from becoming dry\"]', 1, 'b408ceab-70e7-4415-8bc8-a44e1d40137f'),
('9fb8e684-818e-41dc-b59d-416da9fd3f19', 'How does the process of \"sterilization\" differ from \"disinfection\"?', '[\"Disinfection is faster but sterilization is cheaper\",\"Disinfection is for skin, while sterilization is for furniture\",\"Disinfection kills all spores, while sterilization only cleans dirt\",\"Sterilization destroys all microorganisms including spores, while disinfection only kills most pathogens\"]', 3, '265a8637-d8a4-4346-9a76-220c10e72487'),
('a0468a08-1f7b-4d15-92d4-1f519f3dbe16', 'When providing foot care, why is it critical to thoroughly dry the areas between the toes?', '[\"To prevent the skin from cracking\",\"To reduce the risk of fungal infections\",\"To make it easier to apply socks\",\"To stimulate blood circulation\"]', 1, 'b216c7dd-616d-48f7-9c6c-3113e99e4e93'),
('a08bb8a6-4f07-4bc9-b82a-43c157d1006c', 'Which lifestyle factor may help reduce the risk of dementia?', '[\"Avoiding social interaction\",\"Lack of physical activity\",\"Regular exercise, healthy diet, and mental stimulation\",\"Skipping medical checkups\"]', 2, '166bbd14-2963-4869-b865-e693f15b0c68'),
('a1c69c78-ae30-4949-9fe8-2d99cfaf5737', 'Why are communicable infections a major concern specifically in healthcare settings compared to other public areas?', '[\"Because healthcare workers are the only people who can carry pathogens\",\"Because hospitals do not have enough cleaning supplies\",\"Because they can spread quickly among staff and patients who often have weakened immune systems\",\"Because pathogens cannot survive on surfaces in residential homes\"]', 2, '1559396d-9733-4cad-abfe-d57610b7c738'),
('a33d46cf-1c92-4580-87a2-24cc1c2e37d6', 'Which of the statements is false?', '[\"The urine drainage system should hang from the bed frame or chair\",\"The urine drainage system should hang from the bed rail\",\"The drainage system must be off the floor\",\"The urine drainage system must be kept lower than the person’s bladder\"]', 1, '91836b42-cb09-4c0d-8071-eed39f135b57'),
('a3dcbc3e-a2e3-405c-8a83-d44eec9ab829', 'Which of the following is an early sign of dementia?', '[\"Difficulty remembering recent events\",\"Complete loss of movement\",\"Sudden blindness\",\"Immediate inability to speak\"]', 0, '25ff77df-b870-45ce-880e-7a2276cee1be'),
('a5081ced-2ba3-4847-b91d-4f7d02d94a3c', 'Why should caregivers encourage independence in patients?', '[\"To reduce workload\",\"To improve staff efficiency\",\"To maintain physical ability and self-esteem\",\"To avoid communication\"]', 2, '23960445-743b-449c-b910-2fbe5aa23815'),
('a546c4d9-e8cb-4a8f-939e-aed18d51ad25', 'Why is it important to gather all supplies before starting a transfer?', '[\"To leave the patient unattended\",\"To complete the transfer smoothly without interruptions\",\"To reduce communication\",\"To delay the process\"]', 1, '2556291b-0982-48da-beaa-944ee7120230'),
('a6efba28-cbf4-4df2-906e-0337cd9faf43', 'Changes in the body’s endocrine system, respiratory rate, heart rate, and blood pressure do not occur during stress.', '[\"True\",\"False\",\"Sometimes\",\"None of the above\"]', 1, 'f1953582-5ac2-48ea-bfbf-5fc4771f5bf3'),
('a7a9b1e4-ad11-475b-9d89-1bb5a5692867', 'What should you ensure before leaving the resident with the urinal?', '[\"Lights are turned off\",\"Call light and toilet paper are within reach\",\"Door is locked\",\"Bed is lowered completely\"]', 1, 'b91fca78-f656-4275-8725-fd09f80ef5b9'),
('a7ecc207-9bd9-4a6c-b7ae-84e90f7d14fb', 'The two types of communication are:', '[\"Verbal and non-verbal\",\"English and Spanish\",\"1 and 2\",\"None of the above\"]', 0, '272a1a4c-f70f-4684-bb1d-c80a19e881b2'),
('a9c44044-aa2b-46b1-9cab-9736334971cc', 'What is one proper method for removing a bedpan?', '[\"Pull it quickly without warning\",\"Ask the resident to bend knees and lift buttocks slightly\",\"Turn the resident face down\",\"Shake the bedpan loose\"]', 1, 'b374df12-e163-42fa-a7a3-de3fcf52ed6a'),
('ab202448-abd8-4097-912c-fdaa9b8c0c16', 'What is objective information in healthcare reporting?', '[\"Personal opinions about a resident\",\"Information based on direct observation and facts\",\"Feelings expressed by the resident\",\"Assumptions made by caregivers\"]', 1, 'fcb31254-4d0b-466f-9a46-176b4e54a3ab'),
('abf0d0f5-f99a-467f-8e88-10fff754805e', 'What is placed between the restraint and the patient’s skin to prevent irritation?', '[\"Nothing\",\"Plastic covering\",\"Clothing or soft material barrier\",\"Metal support\"]', 2, 'deaf63e7-7806-44f2-92cb-75c1f5c542c5'),
('ac0a7733-b0e1-4041-a868-bf2907ea4fc8', 'Why should wheelchair and bed wheels be locked before transfer?', '[\"To improve appearance\",\"To reduce noise\",\"To prevent movement and ensure safety during transfer\",\"To save time\"]', 2, '15093e57-c621-4c3c-be84-4fe43264b21b'),
('ac57941a-0357-4541-80c9-f19cb6bf2fae', 'Why is maintaining a consistent routine important for people with dementia?', '[\"It increases confusion\",\"It helps reduce anxiety and provides a sense of security\",\"It makes caregivers’ jobs harder\",\"It prevents all memory loss\"]', 1, 'ce53c926-f1e6-417b-b4e7-27339b26254a'),
('aca13431-71b7-4b0f-ae3c-e8ebe7283b11', 'Persons in the denial stage of dying…', '[\"Are angry\",\"Bargain with God\",\"Are calm and quiet\",\"Refuse to believe that they are dying\"]', 3, 'd29c9af2-8cf7-4057-8b6b-a1a0f84ba131'),
('ad07b98c-5eb7-4921-888e-7c3b32df80f7', 'In general, most businesses and professions have a code of ethics for practitioners because:', '[\"It is a religious requirement\",\"It is a business requirement\",\"It increases the credibility of the profession\",\"It decreases legal fees if there is a lawsuit\"]', 2, '901e5737-19aa-41c8-a13a-cc963b5f734c'),
('ad5ea408-c197-4e0e-a414-3b3ddce0fd98', 'Stress is both an emotional and physical response.', '[\"True\",\"False\",\"Sometimes\",\"None of the above\"]', 0, 'f1953582-5ac2-48ea-bfbf-5fc4771f5bf3'),
('ade345bd-0805-4209-b9b8-527909159b06', 'What is the primary purpose of a mechanical lift?', '[\"To move equipment\",\"To safely transfer patients with minimal strain on caregivers\",\"To increase workload\",\"To replace caregivers\"]', 1, '0034615a-ba32-49a4-b579-e9526110f40e'),
('ae17a514-b229-4633-b678-ea18e87a3f66', 'Why is getting enough sleep important for stress management?', '[\"It increases stress\",\"It helps the body and mind recover and function properly\",\"It reduces responsibility\",\"It avoids daily tasks\"]', 1, '39c06649-690a-4b95-900c-d67cce948520'),
('ae4a2ad4-a1b2-42f6-ad94-64158b92b962', 'A resident is on a sodium-controlled diet. Which of the following statements is true?', '[\"High-sodium foods are allowed\",\"Salt is added at the table\",\"Pretzels and potato chips are a good snack\",\"The amount of salt used in cooking is limited\"]', 3, '067af97e-29b0-4d1a-9f2a-76bb5d68f2da'),
('aeb27a25-4d81-49e5-84a5-63fe3534ec94', 'Which of the following is a lateral position?', '[\"Resident is sitting in a 45 to 60 degrees with head elevated\",\"Resident lying on either side\",\"Resident is lying flat on their back\",\"Resident is standing upright\"]', 1, 'd6e515cf-fa77-4a1c-b36d-6ab88db1983f'),
('aef723af-01b0-412f-ab7b-c31a7280e356', 'Why is it critical that a person remains on the floor after a fall until a medical assessment is completed?', '[\"To allow the caregiver time to fill out paperwork\",\"Because moving too quickly could worsen an injury or cause another fall from dizziness\",\"To wait for the person\'s family to arrive\",\"To ensure the floor is cleaned before the person stands up\"]', 1, '7dd84b7e-6ce2-4ead-b72a-caf629db92fa'),
('affe1520-4fb3-473f-bbf9-2dc76bcaa38f', 'The following are examples of stressors.', '[\"Parenthood, divorce, a new job, or losing a job\",\"Independence\",\"Patient’s rights\",\"Ethics\"]', 0, 'f1953582-5ac2-48ea-bfbf-5fc4771f5bf3'),
('b0352875-fd14-4627-97dc-8711be6239cc', 'The most common complication of immobility is…', '[\"Pressure ulcers\",\"Diabetes\",\"Nutrition\",\"Aids/HIV\"]', 0, 'd6e515cf-fa77-4a1c-b36d-6ab88db1983f'),
('b05259f3-ac88-4a81-a071-06148bf3710f', 'What is the correct clinical sequence for using Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)?', '[\"PPE is only effective if worn over personal clothing without washing hands\",\"Gloves should be put on before a gown to ensure the hands are covered\",\"Gowns, masks, and gloves must be used correctly and consistently to provide physical protection\",\"Masks should be removed by touching the front filter surface first\"]', 2, '265a8637-d8a4-4346-9a76-220c10e72487'),
('b095e718-0d65-4929-ad45-0c735c6bcc24', 'Which of the following best describes a stressor?', '[\"A coping skill\",\"Something that causes stress\",\"A medical treatment\",\"A relaxation technique\"]', 1, '8eb9ca88-14a4-4f6d-997a-a2ef6250b057'),
('b10af3dd-b1fd-4b27-aea3-8396760a91ae', 'What does participation in treatment decisions mean?', '[\"Doctors make all decisions alone\",\"Patients can be involved in choices about their care\",\"Families decide everything\",\"Patients must follow all orders\"]', 1, '3fe0b3b1-341a-4e34-b5f7-5f55d9639090'),
('b15b9515-8b2e-4bd0-bec9-466f313c70ee', 'Why should a caregiver avoid letting the patient know respirations are being counted?', '[\"To save time\",\"Because the patient may change their breathing pattern and affect accuracy\",\"To reduce communication\",\"To increase speed\"]', 1, '0a1d08c5-968b-4531-829f-b1f38f2371ee'),
('b164aafb-1228-4afc-825a-96344c569dd9', 'Why must a caregiver check the patient\'s care plan or consult a nurse before using a transfer belt on someone with COPD?', '[\"The belt might cause a skin rash\",\"The belt could interfere with abdominal muscle movement and make breathing more difficult\",\"COPD patients are usually too strong for a transfer belt\",\"Transfer belts are only used for patients with leg injuries\"]', 1, '281a9307-160d-4d86-b335-ed0f83212b43'),
('b16f5305-0010-4ba1-afc9-b467658529d1', 'Why must a scale be set to zero before weighing a patient?', '[\"To save time\",\"To ensure the measurement is accurate and not affected by an incorrect starting point\",\"To reduce workload\",\"To improve appearance\"]', 1, '1fdd9048-c2e0-4125-a91e-19d9e6eb3a5f'),
('b18d9d09-2af4-4986-8154-6ef0f56cd63c', 'Which of the following should be reported after perineal care?', '[\"Clean skin\",\"Normal appearance\",\"Redness or unusual discharge\",\"Dry towel used\"]', 2, 'c83e27ae-9809-405d-9ffb-f9498e983702'),
('b1b3edc4-0ef3-445d-b5e0-ed567919ac15', 'What is negligence in healthcare?', '[\"Intentional harm to a patient\",\"Failing to act carefully, resulting in harm\",\"Providing high-quality care\",\"Following doctor’s orders exactly\"]', 1, '3c98a91c-fff1-4360-8efb-6742f0a3cd78'),
('b21fd9a7-3c62-4610-86b7-7840eccfe45e', 'Why is the use of \"good body mechanics\" emphasized when a caregiver is repositioning a patient for grooming?', '[\"It helps prevent strain or injury to both the caregiver and the patient\",\"It is required by law for every single interaction\",\"It ensures the grooming supplies remain sterile\",\"It makes the grooming process much louder and faster\"]', 0, '76ee044c-6c1e-4dac-b4c6-378f4a555137'),
('b26b67f3-de25-4c74-bb87-0fff7b56a734', 'What is the main benefit of the lateral (side-lying) position?', '[\"It prevents eating\",\"It relieves pressure on the back and improves circulation\",\"It limits breathing\",\"It increases discomfort\"]', 1, '389a7d8d-2938-4604-8d2f-84f846d84e5a'),
('b2f2227a-af3f-405d-86d2-a55d48ab8508', 'What should be done if a patient is too heavy to move safely alone?', '[\"Attempt to lift quickly\",\"Skip the task\",\"Ask for help or use equipment\",\"Pull the patient forcefully\"]', 2, '392fd2f4-79d8-468a-8320-1dae1ea55da0'),
('b3646352-2f09-4f5c-9634-7ee9466adf42', 'Why is accurate height measurement important in healthcare?', '[\"It improves communication\",\"It is only for records\",\"It helps calculate body mass index (BMI) and assess health status\",\"It reduces workload\"]', 2, '1fdd9048-c2e0-4125-a91e-19d9e6eb3a5f'),
('b3cedb92-d416-40a2-9415-504041662f06', 'Where should you aim a fire extinguisher when putting out a fire?', '[\"At the flames\",\"At the ceiling\",\"At the base of the fire\",\"At the smoke\"]', 2, '811051a7-2283-4853-a6c3-b9740b7fe373'),
('b417cb48-4d57-4d35-8801-082c47c11f5d', 'Why should respirations be counted for a full 60 seconds when breathing is irregular?', '[\"To save time\",\"To reduce workload\",\"To obtain a more accurate measurement of uneven breathing patterns\",\"To make the patient comfortable\"]', 2, '0a1d08c5-968b-4531-829f-b1f38f2371ee'),
('b47df6d5-fc63-42cc-95a7-3f8136c9ecd7', 'Which of the following is a non-medical way to help manage pain?', '[\"Ignoring discomfort\",\"Gentle back rubs or massage\",\"Increasing noise levels\",\"Avoiding contact\"]', 1, 'c56fa5fe-0bef-45b6-bce6-0a02d9fbd550'),
('b4b4f95b-4c13-4678-9b04-b71c719a5c3e', 'When using a chemical agent for \"antisepsis,\" where is it specifically designed to be applied?', '[\"To living tissue, such as a patient\'s skin\",\"To metal surgical instruments only\",\"To floors and walls in the hallway\",\"To contaminated bed linens before washing\"]', 0, '265a8637-d8a4-4346-9a76-220c10e72487'),
('b6725816-3611-4ae8-b91d-a2f88a21648e', 'What is the purpose of using pillows during patient positioning?', '[\"To decorate the bed\",\"To increase workload\",\"To maintain alignment and reduce pressure on the body\",\"To restrict movement\"]', 2, '389a7d8d-2938-4604-8d2f-84f846d84e5a'),
('b72c6121-7524-46bd-aafb-5c0fd3864cf3', 'When the patient refuses a bed bath, the nurse aide should…', '[\"Offer the resident a bribe\",\"Wait awhile and then ask the resident again\",\"Remind the resident that people who smell, don’t have friends\",\"Tell the resident that nursing home policy requires daily bathing\"]', 1, '54d5bd94-bfaa-4dbf-bc23-4eb442ca37d5'),
('b7634988-c5a7-4630-8082-14733b9764e5', 'Why must privacy be maintained during elimination care?', '[\"To reduce time spent\",\"To improve efficiency\",\"To protect dignity and emotional well-being\",\"To avoid communication\"]', 2, '59c1a68d-3138-468c-ae91-2bd9e77d34e1'),
('b7ea023b-633c-4372-8e44-b2773987ea94', 'What is the main purpose of communication?', '[\"To entertain people only\",\"To exchange information, ideas, and feelings between individuals \",\"To reduce workload\",\"To avoid interaction\"]', 1, 'c595624f-18fa-4978-960d-601f5743654e'),
('b7fba09c-e79c-4079-ae7f-0d4927b6c8ee', 'What should a caregiver do before repositioning a patient?', '[\"Move the patient quickly\",\"Explain the procedure to the patient\",\"Ignore patient concerns\",\"Leave the room\"]', 1, '8a8303c4-5158-4166-a174-6b970d9d33a5'),
('b832a8db-ee45-4dce-8375-9494fc33a556', 'Which approach is often preferred as the first line of treatment for behavioral symptoms in dementia?', '[\"Antipsychotic medications\",\"Surgical intervention\",\"Non-pharmacological interventions\",\"High-dose sedatives\"]', 2, '2693df92-9de2-4c7d-9039-3b889baef28c'),
('b85916e9-2918-4e39-8342-9b43db1323ca', 'Which action best demonstrates treating a terminally ill resident as a living person?', '[\"Ignoring them if they are unresponsive\",\"Speaking about them instead of to them\",\"Including them in conversations and explaining procedures\",\"Limiting interaction to medical tasks only\"]', 2, 'a96de350-39f0-44e1-84ac-cbfcaa55cd35'),
('b8f7b3d7-0112-41fa-b3cb-642a10a6f471', 'Why must restraints never be tied to the side rails of a bed?', '[\"It makes the bed look untidy\",\"Side rails can move and cause injury to the patient\",\"It is harder to tie knots\",\"It reduces patient comfort\"]', 1, 'deaf63e7-7806-44f2-92cb-75c1f5c542c5'),
('b95a372d-26ee-4af4-9f8e-f94bca06742d', 'Why should patients be weighed at the same time of day using the same scale?', '[\"To delay the process\",\"To reduce communication\",\"To ensure consistency and accurate comparison over time\",\"To increase workload\"]', 2, '1fdd9048-c2e0-4125-a91e-19d9e6eb3a5f'),
('b9e1cb5e-8faf-44d6-9f15-ca4be611290d', 'According to the material, how many older adults aged 65 and older experience a fall each year?', '[\"One out of ten\",\"More than one out of four\",\"Less than five percent\",\"Every other person\"]', 1, '3cf47254-a409-400d-80c9-02d44010d074'),
('ba210759-a7d4-495b-a4c9-ccea65a2e083', 'Which of the following is an example of subjective information?', '[\"A visible rash on the arm\",\"Swelling in the leg\",\"A resident saying they feel pain\",\"Redness of the skin\"]', 2, 'fcb31254-4d0b-466f-9a46-176b4e54a3ab'),
('bab4a692-6a78-43ce-85c4-b09d4d5c7b90', 'Which natural body defense helps prevent microorganisms from entering the body?', '[\"Muscles\",\"Skin acting as a protective barrier\",\"Bones\",\"Hair growth\"]', 1, 'f8710db2-d98a-4e70-aac6-6620637b7333'),
('bb193a4d-7b89-4291-9ba9-36dd2ab94e03', 'What condition may occur if fluid intake exceeds the body’s ability to remove it?', '[\"Dehydration\",\"Malnutrition\",\"Fluid overload with edema\",\"Fever\"]', 2, '23c9dcc6-6116-4dc0-9404-13aacf132101'),
('bb2b4a02-a258-4a8f-a430-d589630be629', 'What should be done if a patient shows signs like dizziness or chest pain during transfer?', '[\"Continue the transfer\",\"Ignore the symptoms\",\"Stop immediately and notify the nurse\",\"Finish quickly\"]', 2, '2556291b-0982-48da-beaa-944ee7120230'),
