('d9c288be-7730-4aac-8012-c0a6cbcf3212', 'What is the primary purpose of leaving slack in the catheter tubing?', '[\"To increase urine flow speed\",\"To prevent tension and pulling at the insertion site\",\"To make the tubing look neat\",\"To reduce the need for cleaning\"]', 1, '62279771-a981-49dc-9603-3e67b191fa70'),
('daeeaa02-1288-4078-85d1-416981a07abb', 'What should a caregiver do if a patient cannot stand for height measurement?', '[\"Skip the measurement\",\"Estimate the height\",\"Use an alternative method such as measuring in bed or using arm span\",\"Ask the patient\"]', 2, '1fdd9048-c2e0-4125-a91e-19d9e6eb3a5f'),
('db728996-51af-407d-b38a-8411b6f8b34b', 'Why must a scale be set to zero before weighing a patient?', '[\"To save time\",\"To ensure the measurement is accurate and not affected by an incorrect starting point\",\"To reduce workload\",\"To improve appearance\"]', 1, '4a08969c-413c-47b6-a033-25020fd1980e'),
('db9667fe-6605-414b-ab81-1908c35df62c', 'In a clinical setting, how do Airborne Precautions differ from Droplet Precautions regarding the environment?', '[\"They require the use of standard cloth gowns only\",\"They allow the door to remain open at all times\",\"They require specialized ventilation systems and N95 respirators\",\"They do not require the caregiver to wash their hands\"]', 2, '799071aa-8ffd-44f6-9eac-13e2a56d71da'),
('dc7ce1f9-b818-4cc9-8481-b0909242251f', 'A resident who is inactive is at risk of constipation. In addition to increased activity and exercise, which of the following actions helps to prevent constipation?', '[\"Adequate fluid intake \",\"Regular mealtimes\",\"High protein diet\",\"Low fiber diet\"]', 0, '067af97e-29b0-4d1a-9f2a-76bb5d68f2da'),
('dcbdfacb-40fb-491d-a06c-7306055d7d24', 'Which statement about falls is false?', '[\"Poor lighting, cluttered floors, and throw rugs may cause falls.\",\"Improper shoes and needing to use the bathroom may cause falls.\",\"Most falls occur between 6:00 pm and 9:00pm\",\"Falls are less likely to occur during shift change\"]', 3, '2d454161-7461-4f34-bb59-00c45483349b'),
('dcc3085c-f86f-4cd3-b528-3f069de4fbcf', 'What is the first step before applying any physical restraint?', '[\"Lock the door\",\"Wash hands thoroughly\",\"Tie the restraint\",\"Raise side rails\"]', 1, 'deaf63e7-7806-44f2-92cb-75c1f5c542c5'),
('dd0f3f5d-e736-49e5-8bab-c11469f0237a', 'How can cultural practices affect a resident’s nutrition?', '[\"They have no impact on eating habits\",\"They determine food preferences and meal practices \",\"They only affect food cost\",\"They eliminate the need for balanced diets\"]', 1, 'c8237a4e-a5c6-44ce-bfbf-7cb1e6093418'),
('dd76832e-1816-4e62-8ebe-36b5feb07a42', 'Which of the following is a good listening behavior?', '[\"Crossing arms and looking away\",\"Interrupting frequently\",\"Facing the speaker and paying attention\",\"Ignoring non-verbal cues\"]', 2, 'c595624f-18fa-4978-960d-601f5743654e'),
('de837b8b-6320-49a7-9feb-66d81853d4d7', 'What is the primary goal of medical asepsis in a healthcare environment?', '[\"To eliminate every single microorganism from the facility\",\"To reduce the number of pathogens and prevent their spread\",\"To replace the need for wearing gloves\",\"To ensure all surfaces are painted with antimicrobial paint\"]', 1, '265a8637-d8a4-4346-9a76-220c10e72487'),
('deec074f-7a24-4eb2-a2ac-4b8f01739453', 'Which of the following is a common indicator that physical elderly abuse is occurring?', '[\"An elderly person with a mental disorder\",\"An elderly person with financial struggles\",\"An elderly person who refuses to accept prescribed medications\",\"An elderly person with unexplained injuries\"]', 3, '54d5bd94-bfaa-4dbf-bc23-4eb442ca37d5'),
('df24790f-a2b1-49af-905c-36b0751a083b', 'Why must a caregiver ask if a patient has eaten or drunk anything before taking an oral temperature?', '[\"To delay the process\",\"Because it affects blood pressure\",\"Because hot or cold substances can alter the reading\",\"To reduce communication\"]', 2, 'e3935e28-e1fd-48fd-964f-d1b5be8d3daa'),
('df8feaa9-41c7-4984-a9d7-86845681d390', 'Which of the following best explains the relationship between understanding the science of disease transmission and practical infection control?', '[\"Scientific knowledge is only useful for those working in laboratory settings\",\"Understanding how diseases spread empowers workers to take necessary precautions in every interaction\",\"Learning the science of infection replaces the need for daily handwashing\",\"Knowledge of transmission is used primarily to reduce the amount of cleaning required\"]', 1, '5e2be435-8690-4235-9548-bc0c6906e02c'),
('dfeda620-ae93-49a9-82cb-e536f8af6ce1', 'If you are present when a person begins to fall, what is the safest physical response you should take?', '[\"Try to catch the person and hold up their full weight\",\"Step back and let the person fall freely to avoid injuring yourself\",\"Ease the person to the floor by controlling the fall and guiding them down\",\"Quickly grab the person\'s arms and pull them upright\"]', 2, '7dd84b7e-6ce2-4ead-b72a-caf629db92fa'),
('e004fce6-a9f2-44b5-85a1-57f1898df086', 'What can be overwhelming when you try to handle it yourself?', '[\"Patient care and hygiene\",\"Transfer\",\"Stress\",\"Doctor’s appointment\"]', 2, 'f1953582-5ac2-48ea-bfbf-5fc4771f5bf3'),
('e085b3a5-1404-4dea-aaef-44b86c6ecc54', 'What is the correct placement of the sling under the patient?', '[\"From head to feet\",\"From shoulders to knees\",\"Only under the back\",\"Only under the legs\"]', 1, '0034615a-ba32-49a4-b579-e9526110f40e'),
('e0edb043-b56d-4504-98d0-4595fe64da42', 'What is the primary reason for modifying food texture in a dysphagia diet?', '[\"To improve food color\",\"To reduce cooking time\",\"To prevent choking and aspiration\",\"To increase fat content\"]', 2, '4fa74711-53a5-4985-b2e6-d5cf499b13bd'),
('e1449732-8405-4972-8dbb-f64a40d7e3c7', 'Why is it important to address a resident by their preferred name?', '[\"To save time\",\"To make communication faster\",\"To show respect and recognize them as an individual\",\"To follow routine only\"]', 2, '66d3683d-f4cd-4558-90f6-e49b39476850'),
('e1a8d38c-461d-4e8b-a030-46e1ea8c9614', 'After completing a transfer, you should…', '[\"Leave the patient\",\"Walk away immediately\",\"Ensure the patient is safe, comfortable, and properly positioned\",\"Ignore the patient\"]', 2, '20efff82-6d52-4bd6-b13a-21418d0239af');
INSERT INTO `Question` (`id`, `text`, `options`, `correctAnswer`, `quizId`) VALUES
('e2c5f9a4-5dfe-4d57-836f-cc559b650276', 'Why must pulse be counted for a full 60 seconds when the rhythm is irregular?', '[\"To save time\",\"To avoid counting errors and obtain a more accurate measurement\",\"To reduce workload\",\"To make it easier\"]', 1, '9efcfbe0-4ab4-4f1d-8a4b-5dde1a3a3af4'),
('e3a2708e-5ed2-4d27-a421-6d1fada4fa61', 'A resident who is incontinent of urine has an increased risk of developing…', '[\"Dementia\",\"Urinary tract infections\",\"Pressure sores\",\"Dehydration\"]', 2, 'd6e515cf-fa77-4a1c-b36d-6ab88db1983f'),
('e4a3f551-ba6b-4c5c-8493-e59dd7975ea5', 'What are height and weight used for in healthcare?', '[\"Only for records\",\"To assess overall health status and physical condition\",\"To replace vital signs\",\"To reduce patient care\"]', 1, '4a08969c-413c-47b6-a033-25020fd1980e'),
('e4c6c5b8-1767-4c7f-846b-6a2312dcd6d7', 'A patient is in a coma. What is most appropriate?', '[\"Speak to the patient as if he can hear what is being said\",\"Avoid verbal stimulation\",\"Limit family visits\",\"Turn on the television\"]', 0, 'd29c9af2-8cf7-4057-8b6b-a1a0f84ba131'),
('e56b167d-15f1-4ea6-a22d-fcaad84028be', 'Mr. Smith does not want lifesaving measures. You…', '[\"Explain to Mr. Smith’s family why he should have lifesaving measures\",\"Respect his decision\",\"Explain to Mr. Smith why lifesaving measures are needed\",\"Tell your friend about Mr. Smith’s decision\"]', 1, '54d5bd94-bfaa-4dbf-bc23-4eb442ca37d5'),
('e59c9b9c-e1d0-451e-98cd-143bcddbbfe7', 'Why is it important for healthcare workers to manage stress?', '[\"To avoid communication\",\"To reduce workload\",\"To maintain quality patient care and personal well-being\",\"To eliminate responsibilities\"]', 2, '8eb9ca88-14a4-4f6d-997a-a2ef6250b057'),
('e5f124dd-3713-48ba-8bd2-35546f1aaf4f', 'The presence of an advance directive helps the staff to recognize that the purpose of this documentation is to:', '[\"Help every person exercise the right to die with dignity\",\"Encourage the person to determine how he or she will die\",\"Allow the patient the right to autonomy\",\"Provide a means to prevent medical malpractice\"]', 0, '067af97e-29b0-4d1a-9f2a-76bb5d68f2da'),
('e63d99bb-8615-47a2-bfdd-fdaf56f7e0fe', 'An advanced directive helps staff recognize:', '[\"The patient’s right to die with dignity\",\"Encourage how a person will die\",\"Allow autonomy\",\"Prevent malpractice\"]', 0, 'd29c9af2-8cf7-4057-8b6b-a1a0f84ba131'),
('e6b2f148-9fd3-42ac-a21e-73d85be5f606', 'When giving hair care, you should:', '[\"Brush or comb from the scalp to the hair ends.\",\"Use a wide-toothed comb for curly hair.\",\"Start at the hair ends and work toward the scalp.\",\"Use a fine-toothed comb for matted hair.\"]', 0, '84f81917-156c-4b77-a41c-8e45dcb9970e'),
('e755dfa0-0d15-4fbf-8b77-4722b169823d', 'What does ethics refer to in healthcare?', '[\"Hospital rules only\",\"Understanding what is right and wrong\",\"Medical equipment usage\",\"Legal punishments\"]', 1, '3c98a91c-fff1-4360-8efb-6742f0a3cd78'),
('e81a93b3-8bc6-4047-9a5c-442a0f024331', 'What is one important step before serving a meal to a resident?', '[\"Give medication\",\"Assist with elimination if needed\",\"Turn off the lights\",\"Start feeding immediately\"]', 1, '5a73afcd-b5f1-4498-91a6-6802c950e230'),
('e867726e-5bb9-4328-998c-3fd029076581', 'Why are open-ended questions important?', '[\"They shorten conversations\",\"They limit responses\",\"They encourage residents to give more detailed information\",\"They confuse residents\"]', 2, 'fcb31254-4d0b-466f-9a46-176b4e54a3ab'),
('e87f7acc-7ec7-4b6f-8c55-6499a3c46ef0', 'A cancer resident is expected to die within a couple of days. Nursing care should focus on:', '[\"Helping the resident through the stages of grief\",\"Providing for the resident’s comfort\",\"Keeping the resident’s care routine\",\"Giving the resident a lot of quiet time\"]', 1, 'd29c9af2-8cf7-4057-8b6b-a1a0f84ba131'),
('e897b15f-2c53-4eeb-ad63-2b2ff7f2aecf', 'The CNA is assigned to care for a Muslim patient. When she enters the room, she realizes that the patient is praying. What action by the CNA is most appropriate?', '[\"The CNA should stay in the room and wait until the patient is finished with their prayers\",\"The CNA should quietly leave the room and give the patient privacy to pray\",\"The CNA should tell the patient that he cannot pray while he is in the hospital\",\"The CNA should interrupt the patient and tell him it is time for his care to be given\"]', 1, '54d5bd94-bfaa-4dbf-bc23-4eb442ca37d5'),
('e8b10cb6-e0ba-4ef1-a5a7-96e79f44c5cc', 'You should provide all the following to the dying resident except:', '[\"Eye care\",\"Oral care\",\"Good skin care\",\"Physical activity\"]', 3, 'd29c9af2-8cf7-4057-8b6b-a1a0f84ba131'),
('e8cd42b2-2e9d-4cf8-8da4-538d9556147a', 'The patient is in a coma after a motor vehicle accident. Which statement regarding communication with the patient is most appropriate?', '[\"Speak to the patient as if he can hear what is being said\",\"Avoid verbal stimulation because of its potential to trigger excitability\",\"Encourage family members to limit visitation to no more than 5 minutes per hour\",\"Turn the television on to stimulate the patient\"]', 0, '272a1a4c-f70f-4684-bb1d-c80a19e881b2'),
('e90950b4-8bb5-4149-9324-b9106246d0c6', 'In which stage of dementia do symptoms begin to noticeably affect daily life?', '[\"Mild cognitive impairment\",\"Mild dementia\",\"Moderate dementia\",\"Severe dementia\"]', 1, 'f7cf8a63-4e75-49d5-918a-6e8dd3e566c3'),
('e923542c-bb4f-443d-abcc-bad054eb210d', 'Insurance companies can have access to the protected health information.', '[\"True\",\"False\",\"Sometimes\",\"None of the above\"]', 0, '11ac83d9-baf5-43d1-a21f-17db499df927'),
('ea18229f-d3c3-4fda-9e28-4ecf6382dbe4', 'How can caregivers help reduce agitation caused by environmental factors?', '[\"Increase noise and activity\",\"Move the person to a quieter, calmer environment\",\"Ignore the surroundings\",\"Turn off all lights\"]', 1, '6d4efbb4-c0de-4659-b30a-9eebb4c7c540'),
('eac21e85-820d-4b5f-a6aa-b2e714a8a42c', 'What is the purpose of providing regular mouth care to a dying resident?', '[\"To improve appetite only\",\"To prevent dryness, discomfort, and infection\",\"To help them speak loudly\",\"To reduce the need for fluids\"]', 1, 'd4ea4a64-767a-485a-a128-e8fae6e109a4'),
('eb89c6b8-cea2-49e5-a54e-f736dad0db8c', 'Why is bathing important for patients in healthcare settings?', '[\"To improve appearance only\",\"To remove sweat, dirt, and bacteria and prevent infections\",\"To reduce caregiver responsibilities\",\"To help patients sleep longer\"]', 1, 'c3ddc9d7-9b76-4097-a19a-e1c8b8b729b4'),
('ec725e33-c58d-46e5-a6e7-6f0e5d4fca93', 'Why is maintaining a consistent daily routine important for individuals with dementia?', '[\"It increases appetite only\",\"It reduces confusion and anxiety by providing predictability\",\"It speeds up recovery\",\"It eliminates the need for caregivers\"]', 1, '2693df92-9de2-4c7d-9039-3b889baef28c'),
('ec8511e2-e231-4908-b2f2-c7e39c54dd6b', 'Why is hand hygiene important before measuring vital signs?', '[\"To follow routine only\",\"To reduce workload\",\"To prevent the spread of infection between caregiver and patient\",\"To delay the process\"]', 2, 'a9481fb6-2854-4cb3-ac30-f2a006c80026'),
('ecb354b7-8719-4960-8113-83a559595f4a', 'When speaking with another person, you…', '[\"Use medical terms that may not be familiar to the person\",\"Mumble your words as you talk\",\"Ask several questions at a time\",\"Speak clearly and distinctly\"]', 3, '272a1a4c-f70f-4684-bb1d-c80a19e881b2'),
('f0123e62-d305-4559-8f15-8a9436dc7d0f', 'Which of the following signs should be reported immediately to the nurse?', '[\"Normal skin color\",\"Redness that does not go away after pressure is relieved\",\"Regular breathing\",\"Dry hair\"]', 1, 'a48b15ad-ec69-4d7a-aae3-43a2ff0b4b0f'),
('f0287c23-20db-43bf-97d8-778cf64775a1', 'Why should caregivers give instructions in small steps to people with dementia?', '[\"To make tasks more confusing\",\"Because the person prefers long explanations\",\"To make tasks easier to understand and follow\",\"To reduce caregiver workload\"]', 2, 'ce53c926-f1e6-417b-b4e7-27339b26254a'),
('f0d6370c-9b70-43c4-aad6-374f71972b70', 'Which statement about transfer/gait belts is false?', '[\"To use the belt safely, follow manufacturer\'s instructions.\",\"Always apply the belt over clothing\",\"Tighten the belt so it is very snug, and breathing is impaired.\",\"Place the belt-buckle off center so it is not over the spine\"]', 2, '2d454161-7461-4f34-bb59-00c45483349b'),
('f20b5162-bd34-49eb-85bf-074968936aa6', 'Why is a sudden change in behavior in a person with dementia important to report?', '[\"It always means the disease is cured\",\"It may be caused by delirium or another medical condition\",\"It is normal and should be ignored\",\"It shows improvement in memory\"]', 1, '02f7a5d5-17d5-45ad-b60b-175e961169eb'),
('f2118f4e-d031-4640-b2bf-93778cb43c38', 'Why must healthcare workers maintain professional boundaries with patients?', '[\"To avoid spending time with them\",\"To prevent conflicts of interest and keep care professional\",\"To make patients more independent\",\"To reduce communication with families\"]', 1, '22ce5fde-f7e9-4180-b8a7-e490c6d72822'),
('f21c97f2-0e8b-4771-96bb-648a0b62dd2a', 'What is the clinical difference between a \"microbe\" and a \"pathogen\"?', '[\"Microbes are only found in hospitals, while pathogens are everywhere\",\"All microbes cause disease, but pathogens are harmless\",\"A microbe is any tiny organism, while a pathogen is a microbe specifically capable of causing illness\",\"There is no difference; the terms are used interchangeably for viruses only\"]', 2, '1559396d-9733-4cad-abfe-d57610b7c738'),
('f2204e7a-c43b-45b5-80da-f65ae78be080', 'Why should caregivers use their leg muscles instead of their back when lifting?', '[\"To move faster\",\"To reduce strain and prevent back injuries\",\"To increase difficulty\",\"To avoid communication\"]', 1, '8872bf64-3d0f-46cf-a9ed-1e93223d41de'),
('f28b6635-42cd-4065-ad9d-f851f229ea66', 'When a patient is placed on Droplet Precautions, what specific PPE is required for a caregiver entering the room?', '[\"A respirator (N95)\",\"A surgical mask\",\"Heavy rubber gloves\",\"No PPE is required\"]', 1, '799071aa-8ffd-44f6-9eac-13e2a56d71da'),
('f2e194c4-f6ba-4f5a-8dca-b3525d269c65', 'What is the correct order of actions in the RACE fire response plan?', '[\"Alarm, Rescue, Confine, Extinguish\",\"Rescue, Alarm, Confine, Extinguish\",\"Rescue, Confine, Alarm, Extinguish\",\"Extinguish, Alarm, Rescue, Confine\"]', 1, '811051a7-2283-4853-a6c3-b9740b7fe373'),
('f33282f6-346a-42d9-b604-72d560feaa2d', 'What is the first step in preparation before assisting with elimination care?', '[\"Gathering supplies\",\"Washing hands\",\"Identifying the resident\",\"Explaining the procedure\"]', 1, '59c1a68d-3138-468c-ae91-2bd9e77d34e1'),
('f5116aa5-ca46-462d-b3da-6a581aa23a81', 'What is the correct way to refer to incontinence garments?', '[\"Diapers\",\"Pads or briefs\",\"Covers\",\"Liners\"]', 1, '25f9a7e4-3ecf-4435-af3b-2a09133a68b8'),
('f5924cbd-44bf-4948-b9f1-736a3e29965e', 'How does personal grooming provide a clinical benefit beyond just cleanliness?', '[\"It acts as a substitute for medical Vital Sign checks\",\"It allows the caregiver to observe the patient\'s body for unusual changes like rashes or sores\",\"It eliminates the need for the patient to use a call light\",\"It is the primary way to determine if a patient needs a new diet\"]', 1, '76ee044c-6c1e-4dac-b4c6-378f4a555137'),
('f64991b4-83ee-4340-ab48-605be5555ce5', 'Why are exercises like Tai Chi and yoga specifically recommended for older adults in fall prevention programs?', '[\"They are high-impact exercises that build bone density quickly\",\"They focus on slow, controlled movements that improve balance and flexibility while being low impact\",\"They are the only exercises that do not require medical supervision\",\"They eliminate the need for using walkers or canes\"]', 1, 'aa49f47d-7374-4647-a3fc-94c3a4182c94'),
('f6e43210-bf8c-469e-9cc7-7d3894494acd', 'Why is the use of \"good body mechanics\" emphasized when a caregiver is repositioning a patient for grooming?', '[\"It is required by law for every single interaction\",\"It helps prevent strain or injury to both the caregiver and the patient\",\"It ensures the grooming supplies remain sterile\",\"It makes the grooming process much louder and faster\"]', 1, 'b408ceab-70e7-4415-8bc8-a44e1d40137f'),
('f790b2da-65d3-4024-a6aa-fc595a736537', 'What is the correct action when a patient feels dizzy during transfer?', '[\"Continue the transfer\",\"Ignore the symptom\",\"Help the patient back to a safe position and stop the transfer\",\"Move faster\"]', 2, '15093e57-c621-4c3c-be84-4fe43264b21b'),
('f7f24a54-d3f1-450e-9eff-9c978d321e8e', 'What is abuse?', '[\"Providing medical care\",\"Intentional mistreatment or harm of another person\",\"Helping a resident with daily tasks\",\"Following facility rules\"]', 1, 'c94d5e14-1342-4995-951c-14928f2ff0e9'),
('f91d2fc5-6627-434e-9b5d-ae88ceea701e', 'How can caregivers maintain a patient’s dignity during end-of-life care?', '[\"Ignore their preferences\",\"Speak and act respectfully and protect privacy\",\"Avoid communication\",\"Rush through care procedures\"]', 1, 'c56fa5fe-0bef-45b6-bce6-0a02d9fbd550'),
('f9aa997b-814b-4779-b7ff-a24a9d975332', 'Which of the following is considered fluid intake?', '[\"Solid bread\",\"Cooked rice\",\"Ice cream that melts at room temperature\",\"Fried meat\"]', 2, '23c9dcc6-6116-4dc0-9404-13aacf132101'),
('f9e391e0-97c6-4ef6-9e38-fa1d942ceb28', 'What should be done after bathing to prevent skin irritation or infection?', '[\"Leave the skin slightly wet\",\"Dry the patient thoroughly, especially in skin folds\",\"Skip drying to save time\",\"Apply cold water\"]', 1, 'c3ddc9d7-9b76-4097-a19a-e1c8b8b729b4'),
('fab1c16c-3e86-4e04-9ca2-e34b0abec73f', 'What should the patient do with their arms before being lifted?', '[\"Hold the caregiver\",\"Leave arms hanging\",\"Cross arms over the chest\",\"Raise arms upward\"]', 2, '0034615a-ba32-49a4-b579-e9526110f40e'),
('faf3c215-68c0-4ff8-bbcb-0f8bf87b6eba', 'What is the caregiver’s role when signs of approaching death are observed?', '[\"Ignore the changes\",\"Panic and alert family immediately\",\"Observe, report changes, and provide comfort care\",\"Stop all communication\"]', 2, 'f5393a13-0fe0-48e0-b793-6c5503390724'),
('fb6fe0b0-d17e-49f3-a14f-36f67680d726', 'How does dementia impact society beyond the individual?', '[\"It has no wider impact\",\"It only affects hospitals\",\"It affects families, caregivers, and healthcare systems emotionally, physically, and financially\",\"It only affects memory\"]', 2, '166bbd14-2963-4869-b865-e693f15b0c68'),
('fc743c1a-11d0-4280-b723-6060aef15f55', 'What is one proper communication practice before starting care?', '[\"Start immediately without speaking\",\"Introduce yourself to the resident\",\"Avoid eye contact\",\"Use slang language\"]', 1, '66d3683d-f4cd-4558-90f6-e49b39476850'),
('fdc0f878-fefe-440c-b3d3-a6413cf6dc06', 'To provide privacy when giving care, you should do the following except:', '[\"Close the room door.\",\"Close the privacy curtain.\",\"Drape the person\'s body with a bath blanket.\",\"Pull the window blinds.\"]', 3, '84f81917-156c-4b77-a41c-8e45dcb9970e'),
('fde08921-8043-4b39-a9b9-a0dbd54e7937', 'A person has dysphagia. The following should be done except…', '[\"Report choking and coughing during the meal\",\"Report difficulty in breathing during a meal at the end of the shift\",\"Report changes in how the person eats\",\"Follow aspiration precaution\"]', 1, '067af97e-29b0-4d1a-9f2a-76bb5d68f2da'),
('fdf2ea45-1c0e-43dc-8f5b-012fb6ad9be8', 'Health care professionals are expected to...', '[\"Never share protected information\",\"Make reasonable efforts to safeguard protected health information\",\"Share protected health information with other healthcare professionals\",\"Only share protected health information with the patient\'s immediate family\"]', 1, '11ac83d9-baf5-43d1-a21f-17db499df927'),
('fe695c27-e8de-4b9d-8534-62f4b9355bc5', 'Which of the following is considered a normal urine characteristic?', '[\"Cloudy with particles\",\"Strong foul odor\",\"Clear and amber color\",\"Dark red color\"]', 2, 'b91fca78-f656-4275-8725-fd09f80ef5b9'),
('fe75b4c1-6203-4a55-aabb-59b384861d56', 'Why is maintaining a balanced diet particularly important in healthcare settings?', '[\"It reduces the need for medication entirely\",\"It ensures patients eat less food\",\"It supports recovery, immunity, and overall well-being under increased physical stress\",\"It eliminates the need for fluids\"]', 2, '830b371f-b69f-41b9-9d04-bee30bc9ba6f'),
('fe8dfd55-3ef8-40b6-82b2-74cffc7b3b56', 'Why should a patient’s head be turned to the side during oral care for an unconscious patient?', '[\"To improve comfort only\",\"To make brushing easier\",\"To prevent choking or aspiration of fluids\",\"To reduce cleaning time\"]', 2, '8c43867b-df17-4281-8327-5afd858ce2cb'),
('fea830df-7458-4760-9f09-db5595a95453', 'What should a caregiver do if they notice a resident\'s fingernails are very long but facility policy does not permit them to trim nails?', '[\"Trim them anyway to help the resident\",\"Ask the resident\'s roommate to trim them\",\"Notify the nurse so appropriate assistance can be provided\",\"Ignore the nails until the resident\'s family visits\"]', 2, 'b216c7dd-616d-48f7-9c6c-3113e99e4e93'),
('fec077ab-de0d-4c80-8656-a142212ba0d7', 'Which of the following is a potential consequence for a caregiver who attempts to stop a fall by catching the full weight of a falling patient?', '[\"Increased muscle strength from the sudden lift\",\"Serious back injuries or muscle strains\",\"A faster medical evaluation for the patient\",\"Improved balance and coordination\"]', 1, '7dd84b7e-6ce2-4ead-b72a-caf629db92fa'),
('ff299113-95ca-4935-b48d-353f70eedf67', 'What is stress?', '[\"Being frightened, excited, worried, confused, in danger, or irritated\",\"The process of feeling well\",\"Refusing care by the patient\",\"None of the above\"]', 0, 'f1953582-5ac2-48ea-bfbf-5fc4771f5bf3'),
('ff2c874e-1447-4a29-9a9f-9785a0db8af1', 'Which of the following is part of the basic ethical principles in nursing?', '[\"Doing no harm\",\"Performing beneficial services\",\"Not switching to a different field of nursing\",\"Remaining loyal to the profession\"]', 2, '901e5737-19aa-41c8-a13a-cc963b5f734c'),
('ff9461bf-8a9c-4b1b-8765-3535340a945d', 'If a person becomes faint and begins to fall, you should do the following except:', '[\"Ease the person to the floor.\",\"Protect the person\'s head.\",\"Let the person get up before the nurse checks him or her.\",\"Help the nurse complete the incident report.\"]', 2, '2d454161-7461-4f34-bb59-00c45483349b');
